# Preview → production

## Rule

1. **Never push or merge to `main`** unless the user explicitly says the preview is OK / ship to production / merge.
2. All site work ships to **`home-b2b-v1`** first; verify on the **active Deploy Preview**.
3. **Current preview (keep PR open — do not merge until user says production):**  
   https://deploy-preview-6--lisenbart.netlify.app  
   After each push, point the user at that URL (wait for Netlify build if needed).
4. If the preview freezes (PR merged/closed), stop using the old `deploy-preview-N` — open a new PR from `home-b2b-v1` and update this rule with the new URL. Do not nag about “new PR” while the current one is open and building.

## Do not

- Fast-forward / merge `home-b2b-v1` → `main` “to be helpful”
- Tell the user to check production when they asked for preview
- Suggest opening another PR while DP6 / the current open PR is still active
